meta {
  name: ProvisionSandbox
  type: grpc
  seq: 1
}

grpc {
  url: {{coreGrpc}}
  method: /dop.v1.ExecutionService/ProvisionSandbox
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  x-actor-id: {{actorId}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
  x-request-id: {{$guid}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {
      "demand_id": "{{demandId}}",
      "min_tier": "ISOLATION_TIER_NAMESPACE",
      "idempotency_key": "{{$guid}}"
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  **`min_tier` is DECLARED, never presumed.** Omitting it returns
  `InvalidArgument`: the substrate does not choose isolation for you. Asking for a
  tier the substrate does not offer returns `FailedPrecondition` with the list of
  what there is — refusing is better than delivering less in silence.

  The tiers: `hardware`, `kernel_emulated`, `namespace`.

  The sandbox is born with a workspace at `/workspace`, and that is what SURVIVES
  the suspension. Destroying is irreversible and takes the workspace with it.
}
